**What I changed**

- **`src/csv.ts`** (new): `parseCsv(text)` — line-based CSV parser. Splits on `\n`, strips a trailing `\r` per line (so `\r\n` works); a field that starts with `"` keeps commas literal until the closing quote, and `""` inside quotes is one quote. Trailing newline produces no empty final row; empty input → `[]`.
- **`src/cli.ts`**: added a `--json` branch before the usage fallback. Empty input or header-only → `[]\n` code 0; mismatched data-row field count → one line `error: line N has X fields, expected Y\n` with N the physical 1-based line (header = 1), code 1, no JSON; otherwise `JSON.stringify(objects) + '\n'`, code 0. Usage line updated to `csvtool --upper | --count | --json`, code 2 unchanged.
- **`src/csv.test.ts`** (new, 5 tests) and **`src/cli.test.ts`** (+6 tests), in the existing `bun:test` style.

